# The ledger of `image/png`: what Go's `image/png` (Go 1.27) and Python's
# Pillow (its PNG plugin) let a program do with PNG, one block per
# capability, and what Rebel answers. Go's list is this machine's,
# `go doc -all image/png`, 2026-11-18. Pillow is not installed here, so its
# names are those of its documented API, unread by `dir()`. Rust's standard
# library has no PNG: `-` in every block.
#
# The expected pixels of the tests are Go's: files made by Go's encoder and
# by a writer of PNG in Go for what Go's encoder never writes (gray of 1, 2
# and 4 bits, gray and alpha, tRNS, Adam7, every filter, chunks around the
# data), each decoded by Go's png.Decode on 2026-11-18. Every file this
# package writes, of the eight formats and indexed, was read back by Go's
# png.Decode the same day, pixel for pixel equal.

capability png/decode  a PNG file read into an image
  heroes  image/png.decode, image/png.decode_with, image/png.decode_image, image/png.decoding, image/png.DecodeOptions, image/png.Png
  go      Decode, FormatError, FormatError.Error, UnsupportedError, UnsupportedError.Error
  rust    -
  python  Image.open, PngImagePlugin.PngImageFile
  note    every colour type and depth: a gray of 1, 2 or 4 bits scaled to 8 as Go scales it, a palette looked up, tRNS made alpha (Go's choice; Pillow keeps it in info), 16 bits kept. Go accepts an index past the palette and an unknown critical chunk; the PNG specification calls both errors, so they fail `invalid` and `unsupported` here, the one place this package and Go answer otherwise

capability png/interlace-read  an Adam7-interlaced file read
  heroes  image/png.decode
  go      Decode
  rust    -
  python  Image.open
  note    -

capability png/interlace-write  an image written interlaced
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    neither Go nor, by its documentation, Pillow writes one

capability png/info  the size and format read without the pixels
  heroes  image/png.info_of, image/png.Info
  go      DecodeConfig
  rust    -
  python  Image.open (lazy: size and mode before load)
  note    -

capability png/limits  a file that claims a huge image refused before it is allocated
  heroes  image/png.decode with image.Limits
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS, PngImagePlugin.MAX_TEXT_CHUNK, PngImagePlugin.MAX_TEXT_MEMORY
  note    the image data is inflated to exactly the size the header implies, a text's compression to the limit the caller gives `texts_of`

capability png/encode  an image written as PNG
  heroes  image/png.encode, image/png.encoding, image/png.EncodeOptions
  go      Encode, Encoder, Encoder.Encode, Encoder.CompressionLevel
  rust    -
  python  Image.save(format="PNG"), PngImagePlugin._save
  note    colour type 0, 2, 4 or 6 as the format says, 8 or 16 bits. Go writes an opaque RGBA image as RGB; here a format is written as it is, `image.convert` first to drop an alpha that is all opaque

capability png/compression-level  how hard the image data is compressed
  heroes  image/png.EncodeOptions.level
  go      CompressionLevel, DefaultCompression, NoCompression, BestSpeed, BestCompression
  rust    -
  python  Image.save(compress_level=), Image.save(optimize=)
  note    0 to 9, as zlib's; Go's four names are 6, 0, 1 and 9 here

capability png/filters  each row's filter chosen
  heroes  image/png.Filter, image/png.EncodeOptions.filter
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    none, sub, up, average, Paeth, or the adaptive choice (least sum of the bytes read as signed), which is what Go does and what libpng does by default

capability png/indexed  an image of a palette written, at the fewest bits an index needs
  heroes  image/png.encode_indexed, image/png.Png.palette
  go      Encode of a Paletted image
  rust    -
  python  Image.save of a "P" image, Image.save(bits=), Image.save(transparency=)
  note    1, 2, 4 or 8 bits for 2, 4, 16 or 256 colours, as Go chooses; alpha in tRNS up to the last entry that is not opaque

capability png/chunks  ancillary chunks kept or dropped when reading, and written
  heroes  image/png.Chunk, image/png.Keep, image/png.DecodeOptions.keep, image/png.EncodeOptions.chunks, image/png.Png.chunks
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.info, PngImagePlugin.PngInfo, PngInfo.add, Image.save(pnginfo=), Image.save(exif=), Image.save(icc_profile=), Image.save(dpi=)
  note    kept as the file holds them, their place before or after the image data kept; written where PNG wants them, the colour chunks before PLTE. A chunk of the program's own is four letters beginning in lower case

capability png/text  text chunks read and written
  heroes  image/png.texts_of, image/png.text_chunk, image/png.Text
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.text, PngImagePlugin.PngInfo.add_text, PngInfo.add_itxt, PngImagePlugin.iTXt
  note    tEXt and zTXt read as Latin-1, iTXt as UTF-8; written as tEXt for ASCII and iTXt otherwise, uncompressed. Pillow writes zTXt where asked; compressed writing is pending under png/text-compressed

capability png/text-compressed  a text chunk written compressed
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  PngInfo.add_text(zip=True), PngInfo.add_itxt(zip=True)
  note    -

capability png/colour-chunks  gamma, chromaticities, sRGB and ICC applied to the pixels
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.info["gamma"], Image.info["icc_profile"]
  note    the chunks are kept as bytes; applying them is colour management (image's ledger, image/colour-management)

capability png/apng  animated PNG read and written
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.seek on an APNG, Image.n_frames, Image.save(save_all=True, duration=, loop=, disposal=, blend=)
  note    its acTL, fcTL and fdAT chunks are kept as chunks today

dropped
  go      EncoderBuffer, EncoderBufferPool, Encoder.BufferPool: buffers reused between encodings, which a value of the language cannot share
  python  Image.save(dictionary=): a zlib preset dictionary, which a PNG reader cannot be given
